{"id": "EUVD-2026-76433", "enisaUuid": "d0c46ecd-0f4b-3094-aa84-878aeec71f9e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsvcrdma: Use svc_xprt_put to free listener on create failure\n\nsvc_rdma_create() calls kfree(cma_xprt) when\nsvc_rdma_create_listen_id() fails. svc_xprt_init() has already\nacquired a net namespace reference via get_net_track(); kfree\nbypasses svc_xprt_free() which releases it.\n\nReplace the kfree() with svc_xprt_put() so the kref_init birth\nreference drops to zero and svc_xprt_free() dispatches\nsvc_rdma_free() to clean up properly. sc_cm_id is still NULL\nat that point; the preceding patch added the necessary NULL\nguard in svc_rdma_free().\n\nsvc_xprt_free() also drops the module reference via\nmodule_put(), but the caller _svc_xprt_create() does the same\non xpo_create failure, double-putting the single\ntry_module_get() it acquired. Take a compensating\n__module_get() before the svc_xprt_put() to keep the count\nbalanced, matching the convention in svc_rdma_accept()'s error\npath.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e35ec558b8cece9399a50141ecaeadbdb8768dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee70d690b5544b736706a9a5796aafb634013f54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e68380710fc970e07610b2f42594575ad35fdb1c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac1dd6002f758ab7dd3e737757e5a1bb1c0b38d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e346ef7bcb137f50c49f969330ab7dcf64ea1654"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89527", "GHSA-h2xv-x4xq-mhh8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1e795c6d-9551-3c80-8bb2-1dc671ced7a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.37"}, {"id": "35da4612-a0c1-3682-b3f8-84dac1308670", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8518bdac8e85f6580ea3f586adf396cd472bc <ee70d690b5544b736706a9a5796aafb634013f54"}, {"id": "3e422ed9-aa39-3cf2-9e12-e9e76cc9b880", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8518bdac8e85f6580ea3f586adf396cd472bc <e346ef7bcb137f50c49f969330ab7dcf64ea1654"}, {"id": "3e9d408e-b8ed-31a3-9dea-44c02f999445", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8518bdac8e85f6580ea3f586adf396cd472bc <e68380710fc970e07610b2f42594575ad35fdb1c"}, {"id": "45438b4b-5236-3ea0-b567-7111f7c8dfda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8518bdac8e85f6580ea3f586adf396cd472bc <ac1dd6002f758ab7dd3e737757e5a1bb1c0b38d6"}, {"id": "59b16792-ddee-31c3-8759-e6774d911267", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "6d23b6d0-8ae2-3588-b752-6c3b9953172d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7eeda756-5c14-3808-a648-ddcdfea5904c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "831545bb-0d40-3fe5-b555-838843e91801", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "9fde110f-7ea2-3212-a661-524849b2b96a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "cbd09444-b311-3232-8edd-d86eed528403", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e7241eea-3fdc-34ef-b3af-0a4ec498e7c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4fb8518bdac8e85f6580ea3f586adf396cd472bc <2e35ec558b8cece9399a50141ecaeadbdb8768dc"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "53b79474-0e79-3030-bc12-bfa668ebca65", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}